-- title:
--   Entireness of non-trivial narrow ray class L-series (Hecke)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $\mathfrak f$ be a nonzero ideal of $\mathcal O_K$. Write $\mathrm{NarrowRayClassGroup}\,K\,\mathfrak f$ for the quotient of the subgroup `coprimeToModulus` of the units of the group of fractional ideals of $K$ — those invertible fractional ideals $I$ whose valuation `FractionalIdeal.count` at every height-one prime dividing $\mathfrak f$ vanishes — by the subgroup induced on it by `narrowRaySubgroup`, the subgroup generated by `narrowRaySet` $K\,\mathfrak f$. Let $\chi$ be a monoid homomorphism from this group to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi \neq 1$, and let $S$ be a finite set of real infinite places of $K$ such that [`M4aP2.IsParity`](def/NumberField_RayCharacterData.html#L26) holds: for every nonzero $\alpha \in \mathcal O_K$ with $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak f$, the value `chiIdeal` of $\chi$ on the fractional ideal generated by $\alpha$ (that is, $\chi$ of the class of that ideal when it is coprime to $\mathfrak f$, and $0$ otherwise) equals $\prod_{v \in S} \operatorname{sign}(v(\alpha))$ computed through the real embeddings attached to the places in $S$. Then there is a function $g \colon \mathbb C \to \mathbb C$, differentiable on all of $\mathbb C$, with $g(s) = \sum_{C}' \chi(C)\,\mathrm{rayZeta}\,K\,\mathfrak f\,C\,(s)$, the narrow ray class $L$-series [`M4aTorus.rayClassLSeries`](def/NumberField_CompletedRayL.html#L23), for every $s$ with $\operatorname{Re} s > 1$.
--
--   This is Hecke's theorem that the $L$-series of a non-trivial narrow ray class character continues to an entire function, in the form of an entire function agreeing with the Dirichlet series in the half-plane of convergence. It is used to obtain holomorphy, and hence local boundedness, of such $L$-series near $s = 1$, in the estimates for sums of $\mathrm{N}\mathfrak a^{-\sigma}$ over ideals of cyclotomic fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_exists_differentiable_eq_rayClassLSeries_of_ne_one.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_CompletedRayL
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_RayCharacterData

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open NumberField NumberField.InfinitePlace Deep.NTSupply

theorem NumberField.exists_differentiable_eq_rayClassLSeries_of_ne_one
    (K : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] (𝔣 : Ideal (𝓞 K)) (h𝔣 : 𝔣 ≠ ⊥)
    (χ : NarrowRayClassGroup K 𝔣 →* ℂ) (hχ : χ ≠ 1)
    (S : Finset {w : InfinitePlace K // w.IsReal}) (hpar : M4aP2.IsParity K 𝔣 χ S) :
    ∃ g : ℂ → ℂ, Differentiable ℂ g ∧
      ∀ s : ℂ, 1 < s.re → g s = M4aTorus.rayClassLSeries K 𝔣 χ s := by sorry
